I love it.
我太喜欢这样了

5
00:00:14,165 --> 00:00:15,166
This is so great.
这感觉太棒了

6
00:00:15,166 --> 00:00:17,488
And I'm so excited because you have a new book coming out.
而且我特别兴奋 因为你们有一本新书要出版了

7
00:00:17,488 --> 00:00:18,949
Why am I like this?
我为什么会这样？

8
00:00:18,949 --> 00:00:30,863
Why am It was really, it was actually really intense.
为什么我……那段经历真的很强烈 实际上非常激烈

9
00:00:30,863 --> 00:00:34,344
And so you basically sent this 22 year old Sabrina.
所以你基本上是发给了当时 22 岁的萨布丽娜……

10
00:00:34,344 --> 00:00:35,265
I was like 24.
我当时大概 24 岁

11
00:00:35,265 --> 00:00:36,285
Okay, 24.
好吧 24 岁

12
00:00:36,285 --> 00:00:40,687
So 20 would take us back to 24 year old, Sabrina, you sent 170.
所以说回 24 岁的萨布丽娜 你发了 170 多条……

13
00:00:40,687 --> 00:00:43,167
And I had to read it again.
我不得不重新读了一遍

14
00:00:43,167 --> 00:00:44,768
I Was like, is this an exaggeration?
我当时想 这是不是夸张了？

15
00:00:44,768 --> 00:00:45,889
Is this true?
这是真的吗？

16
00:00:45,889 --> 00:00:48,089
Like, is she is this sarcasm?
就好像 她是认真的还是在讽刺？

17
00:00:48,089 --> 00:00:52,391
You sent 173 texts to a guy that you where seeing,
你给你正在约会的一个男人发了 173 条短信

18
00:00:52,391 --> 00:00:55,870
and had a who was based essentially rejecting you.
而他基本上是在拒绝你

19
00:00:55,870 --> 00:01:00,011
And you had a full blown meltdown.
然后你彻底崩溃了

20
00:01:00,011 --> 00:01:06,471
And, you know, when I was reading it,
而且 你知道 当我读到这里时

21
00:01:06,471 --> 00:01:10,212
it was just, I don't know, I just it was so well,
我不知道 我只是觉得……

22
00:01:10,212 --> 00:01:12,332
it of course, highly entertaining,
这当然极具娱乐性

23
00:01:12,332 --> 00:01:14,474
because you're like, here's the train wreck that I was.
因为你会想：看啊 这就是我当年的惨状

24
00:01:14,474 --> 00:01:15,534
And you know you're kind of
你知道 你就像是

25
00:01:15,534 --> 00:01:18,354
like reading this kind of train wreck happening.
在看着一场正在发生的灾难

26
00:01:18,354 --> 00:01:20,715
But I don't know, also felt so sad,
但我不知道 同时也觉得好悲伤

27
00:01:20,715 --> 00:01:24,968
because I think that I don't think I've every sent
因为我觉得我以前从来没发过

28
00:01:24,968 --> 00:01:26,830
173 texts before, I'm not going to lie.
173 条短信 说实话

29
00:01:28,632 --> 00:01:32,337
However, I have like that anxiety
然而 我也有过你

30
00:01:32,337 --> 00:01:37,882
that you where feeling and just like I related to that.
当时那种焦虑 我对此感同身受

31
00:01:37,882 --> 00:01:41,224
And I think that there's a lot of people who do things like this.
而且我觉得有很多人都会做出这种事

32
00:01:41,224 --> 00:01:43,584
So will you just take us through this story?
所以你能给我们讲讲这个故事吗？

33
00:01:43,584 --> 00:01:45,446
Because I think it's an important one.
因为我觉得这是一个很重要的故事

34
00:01:45,446 --> 00:01:48,967
I wish I could lie to you and be like, oh, I've only done that once.
我也希望自己能对你撒谎说：“哦 我只干过一次 ”

35
00:01:48,967 --> 00:01:50,947
I have not done that ones.
但我真的不止干过一次

36
00:01:50,947 --> 00:01:52,209
I tried to find the messages,
我找过聊天记录

37
00:01:52,209 --> 00:01:55,150
and than God my iPhone did not save a lot these other texts.
幸好 iPhone 没存太多这类短信

38
00:01:56,211 --> 00:01:57,313
I was manic.
我当时处于狂躁状态

39
00:01:57,313 --> 00:02:01,218
I remember doing that from even when I was like 16, 17, 18,
我记得从我 16、17、18 岁的时候就开始这样了

40
00:02:01,218 --> 00:02:05,185
when texting started to become more like prevalent in our society.
当时短信开始在我们社会中变得更加普遍

41
00:02:05,185 --> 00:02:06,707
And like once I got an iPhone
而且自从我有了 iPhone 以后

42
00:02:06,707 --> 00:02:10,683
when I Because I saw it as like, I need safety.
因为我把它看作是……我需要安全感

43
00:02:10,683 --> 00:02:13,265
I need you to tell me I will be okay.
我需要你告诉我我会没事的

44
00:02:13,265 --> 00:02:15,687
And so Teddy and I where dating for like two months.
我和泰迪大概约会了两个月

45
00:02:15,687 --> 00:02:17,229
It was a very casual fling.
那只是一段非常随意的露水情缘

46
00:02:17,229 --> 00:02:18,689
It wasn't anything serious.
根本算不上什么认真的关系

47
00:02:18,689 --> 00:02:21,952
Truth be told, I did not even really like this guy that much.
老实说 我甚至并没有那么喜欢这个男人

48
00:02:21,952 --> 00:02:26,034
But I was not in a place mentally where I could challenge that through.
但我当时的心理状态根本无法让我理清这一切

49
00:02:26,034 --> 00:02:27,896
I was just in this, I needs to be safe.
我当时只陷入了这种念头：我需要安全感

50
00:02:27,896 --> 00:02:29,018
I needs have somebody like me.
我需要有人喜欢我

51
00:02:29,018 --> 00:02:30,300
Please pick me.
求求你选我吧

52
00:02:30,300 --> 00:02:34,581
And when I found out that this other girl that I knew was also dating him,
当我发现我认识的另一个女孩也在跟他约会时

53
00:02:34,581 --> 00:02:38,003
this light bulb went off in my head of like, I have to win.
我脑子里“叮”地亮起了一盏灯 觉得我必须赢

54
00:02:38,003 --> 00:02:39,465
I have be the one that he picks.
我必须是他选中的那个人

55
00:02:39,465 --> 00:02:41,226
It cannot be her.
绝不能是她

56
00:02:41,226 --> 00:02:42,086
And she was beautiful
而且她很漂亮

57
00:02:42,086 --> 00:02:43,146
and she was everything, right?
她简直完美 对吧？

58
00:02:43,146 --> 00:02:43,706
All these things.
各种条件都很好

59
00:02:43,706 --> 00:02:45,869
And my insecurities where just rearing their ugly head
我的不安全感开始作祟

60
00:02:45,869 --> 00:02:49,531
because she was tall and blonde and think and beautiful and great career.
因为她高挑金发、身材纤细、漂亮且事业有成

61
00:02:49,531 --> 00:02:51,831
And I felt like a shell of a human of myself.
而我觉得自己连个人的空壳都不如

62
00:02:51,831 --> 00:02:56,297
And when he just told me, hey, this isn't going to work.
而当他对我说 嘿 我们这样行不通时……

63
00:02:56,297 --> 00:02:57,979
I think the average person, you can be bummed.
我觉得普通人遇到这事 你可能会沮丧

64
00:02:57,979 --> 00:02:58,620
You can be sad.
你可能会难过

65
00:02:58,620 --> 00:03:00,741
You might maybe send a few texts being like, hey, are you sure?
你可能只会发几条短信说：嘿 你确定吗？

66
00:03:00,741 --> 00:03:01,823
Can we talk about this?
我们能谈谈吗？

67
00:03:01,823 --> 00:03:03,745
Maybe the person says no.
也许对方说不行

68
00:03:03,745 --> 00:03:04,686
You call your friends.
然后你给朋友打电话

69
00:03:04,686 --> 00:03:05,586
You deal with it.
事情就这么过去了

70
00:03:06,689 --> 00:03:08,230
I didn't have anybody I could turn to.
但我当时没有任何可以倾诉的人

71
00:03:08,230 --> 00:03:09,252
I genuinely didn't.
我是真的没有

72
00:03:09,252 --> 00:03:12,373
I had my family telling me I was too much and to chill out,
家人说我太作、让我冷静

73
00:03:12,373 --> 00:03:13,675
and that never works when you have
焦虑时这根本没用 当你

74
00:03:13,675 --> 00:03:16,296
a lot of anxiety, and I was stuck in my own heard.
有严重焦虑时 我当时深陷思绪出不来

75
00:03:16,296 --> 00:03:17,657
And so my thought process,
所以我的思维过程……

76
00:03:17,657 --> 00:03:20,961
like I'll never forget just literally hitting the wall
我永远不会忘记那种简直像撞到墙上、

77
00:03:20,961 --> 00:03:22,961
and feeling like someone pushed me up against it
感觉有人把我推到墙角的感觉

78
00:03:22,961 --> 00:03:24,924
and like I lost all of my breath.
感觉我整个人都喘不过气来

79
00:03:24,924 --> 00:03:27,346
And I just kept texting and texting
然后我就不停地发信息

80
00:03:27,346 --> 00:03:29,366
and because I genuinely believed
因为我真的相信

81
00:03:29,366 --> 00:03:32,669
on the other side of the next message, that was going to be the one.
下一条信息的另一端 就会是那个转折

82
00:03:32,669 --> 00:03:39,256
That was going And as we know, the spoiler alert is like it didn't.
就会是……如我们所知 剧透一下 并没有

83
00:03:39,256 --> 00:03:40,776
It never does.
从来都没有

84
00:03:40,776 --> 00:03:41,896
And when we where done,
等我们结束这一切

85
00:03:41,896 --> 00:03:43,757
by the time I was done and I woke up in the morning,
醒来已是清晨

86
00:03:43,757 --> 00:03:47,959
this hangover, realizing what I had just done and kept texting him.
宿醉让我意识到自己刚做了什么 还一直在给他发信息

87
00:03:47,959 --> 00:03:49,619
The irony is we didn't speak after that.
讽刺的是 在那之后我们就再也没说过话

88
00:03:49,619 --> 00:03:50,819
He never answered.
他再也没有回过信息

89
00:03:50,819 --> 00:03:54,541
Two years later, two or three years later we rematched again on an app.
两年后 两三年后 我们在一个交友软件上又重新匹配到了

90
00:03:54,541 --> 00:03:56,080
Wow, no way.
哇 不是吧

91
00:03:56,080 --> 00:03:58,842
Yeah, and we went out to dinner and we talked,
对 然后我们一起出去吃晚饭 聊了聊

92
00:03:58,842 --> 00:04:00,622
like we just briefly talked about it.
就稍微提了一下这事

93
00:04:00,622 --> 00:04:01,483
He didn't even clock it.
他甚至都没注意到

94
00:04:01,483 --> 00:04:02,842
he didn't really even think anything of it.
他真的根本没把这当回事

95
00:04:02,842 --> 00:04:05,259
And he's like, I've had women do that to me before.
他还说：“我以前也遇到过女生对我这样 ”

96
00:04:05,259 --> 00:04:06,181
And I'll never forget.
而我永远都不会忘记

97
00:04:06,181 --> 00:04:08,522
And he was like, you know, would you be open to dating again?
然后他说：“你知道吗 你还愿意重新开始约会吗？”

98
00:04:08,522 --> 00:04:10,746
And I was like oh, I'm not interested in you at all.
我说：“哦 我对你一点兴趣都没有 ”

99
00:04:10,746 --> 00:04:11,806
I was, like, I think you're lovely.
我说：“我觉得你人挺好的 ”

100
00:04:11,806 --> 00:04:12,568
You're so nice.
你人很好

101
00:04:12,568 --> 00:04:13,528
That's wild.
太疯狂了

102
00:04:13,528 --> 00:04:14,909
Wait, how many years have passed?
等等 过去多少年了？

103
00:04:14,909 --> 00:04:16,512
About two or three, something like that.
大概两三年吧 差不多

104
00:04:16,512 --> 00:04:18,514
And I think he was open to date again.
而且我觉得他是愿意再次约会的

105
00:04:18,514 --> 00:04:19,113
He was open.
他是愿意的

106
00:04:19,113 --> 00:04:22,297
I think that was his code word of, like we should be intimate again.
我觉得那是他的暗号 意思是“我们应该再次亲热”

107
00:04:22,297 --> 00:04:23,379
Like let's be physical.
就是发生点肢体关系

108
00:04:23,379 --> 00:04:24,959
That was really fun.
那挺有意思的

109
00:04:24,959 --> 00:04:25,980
I just had no desire.
但我就是一点欲望都没有

110
00:04:25,980 --> 00:04:27,201
I wasn't interested in him.
我对一点都不感兴趣

111
00:04:27,201 --> 00:04:29,101
And really, all of that is to say
说到底

112
00:04:29,101 --> 00:04:32,403
is that the reason I started the book with that story
我之所以用那个故事作为书的开篇

113
00:04:32,403 --> 00:04:34,884
was because I wanted to one meet people where they're at, right?
是因为首先我想做到感同身受 对吧？

114
00:04:34,884 --> 00:04:37,264
Like, there's no same in the way that we used to behave,
我们过去的行为并不可耻

115
00:04:37,264 --> 00:04:38,904
but I want to learn from it.
希望能吸取教训

116
00:04:38,904 --> 00:04:41,406
But to to really emphasize it had nothing to do with him.
其次是真正强调 这和他本人毫无关系

117
00:04:41,406 --> 00:04:42,107
Yeah, right.
对 没错

118
00:04:42,107 --> 00:04:43,586
We you and I off camera have spoken
私下里 你和我深入探讨过

119
00:04:43,586 --> 00:04:46,928
so extensively about the narratives and the story that we create,
我们创造的那些叙事和故事

120
00:04:46,928 --> 00:04:50,709
and how we believe that and we genuinely can see our lives through that.
以及我们如何坚信它们 并通过这些滤镜来看待我们的生活

121
00:04:50,709 --> 00:04:52,149
And for him, he was just another
对他而言 他只是另一个

122
00:04:52,149 --> 00:04:54,430
representation of I'm going to be abandoned and left.
“将被抛弃和留下”的具象化代表

123
00:04:54,430 --> 00:04:57,911
And I couldn't sit with that because what did that mean about me?
我无法接受这种感觉 因为那意味着我是个什么样的人？

124
00:04:57,911 --> 00:04:59,031
Right.
对的

125
00:04:59,031 --> 00:05:00,413
Well, you know, there's something else
其实你知道 还有一件事

126
00:05:00,413 --> 00:05:02,273
about the story that really struck me,
关于这个故事深深触动了我

127
00:05:02,273 --> 00:05:07,293
which was that you had said, you'd been sleeping together,
就是你提到你们不仅发生过关系

128
00:05:07,293 --> 00:05:10,355
but also watching movies together.
还一起看电影

129
00:05:10,355 --> 00:05:13,415
So obviously having sleepovers, I'm assuming.
所以显然 我猜你们经常留宿过夜

130
00:05:13,415 --> 00:05:15,637
And yet it's still casual.
然而这竟然还只是“随便玩玩”

131
00:05:17,600 --> 00:05:20,603
So whereas, you know, the intense meltdown,
所以尽管你知道 那种剧烈的情绪崩溃、

132
00:05:20,603 --> 00:05:25,266
the 173 texts might be considered extreme.
发 173 条短信可能被视为极端行为

133
00:05:25,266 --> 00:05:28,269
I don't think that having anxiety
但我认为产生焦虑……

134
00:05:28,269 --> 00:05:30,812
about being rejected by someone
是因为担心被某个人拒绝

135
00:05:31,812 --> 00:05:34,836
who you've been regularly having sleepovers with
而这个人你经常跟他留宿过夜、

136
00:05:34,836 --> 00:05:39,199
and watching movies with and like bonding that way.
一起看电影、有着这种情感羁绊

137
00:05:39,199 --> 00:05:41,901
I don't think that that is extreme.
我不觉得这有什么极端的

138
00:05:41,901 --> 00:05:45,564
I don't understand how people don't have anxiety about that.
我不理解为什么有人面对这种情况会不感到焦虑

139
00:05:45,564 --> 00:05:47,665
And I think that's a very important thing to hone in on,
我认为这是一个非常重要、需要聚焦的痛点：

140
00:05:47,665 --> 00:05:49,666
which is that why have we, as a society,
为什么我们作为社会的一员

141
00:05:49,666 --> 00:05:51,127
why do we put the pressure on ourselves
要给自己施加压力

142
00:05:51,127 --> 00:06:09,668
to not get emotionally involved
要求自己对...保持情感隔离

143
00:06:09,668 --> 00:06:13,970
and connected and attached to someone who we are regularly sleeping with
不去和经常发生关系的人建立连结和依恋？

144
00:06:13,970 --> 00:06:17,810
and do I'm sorry, but like, laying in bed and watching a movie together.
而且——抱歉——就像躺在床上一起看电影这种事

145
00:06:17,810 --> 00:06:20,531
To me, that's like relationship status, very intimate.
对我来说 那就是恋爱状态 非常亲密

146
00:06:20,531 --> 00:06:24,031
It's very intimate, it's actually very intimate cook together.
这非常亲密 一起做饭其实也非常亲密

147
00:06:24,031 --> 00:06:26,773
Yeah, we would do stuff like I would go to his house after work,
对 我下班后会去他家

148
00:06:26,773 --> 00:06:29,574
I'd bring my dog because the daycare was right by his house.
我会带上狗 因为日托就在他家附近

149
00:06:29,574 --> 00:06:31,874
I would just hang out right and we would be there all night.
我就顺便去待一会儿 然后我们就在那儿待一整晚

150
00:06:31,874 --> 00:06:34,783
Sometimes I'd sleep over sometimes I go home right at the dog.
有时候我留宿 有时候我带着狗直接回家

151
00:06:34,783 --> 00:06:35,805
That's a relationship.
这就是恋爱关系

152
00:06:37,045 --> 00:06:38,028
Essentially, right?
本质上就是 对吧？

153
00:06:38,028 --> 00:06:39,569
But no, but it really truly is.
不 真的完全就是

154
00:06:39,569 --> 00:06:51,146
It's a Boyfriend, girlfriend, girlfriend.
这就是男朋友、女朋友……

155
00:06:51,146 --> 00:06:52,067
Girlfriend, whatever.
女朋友 随便怎么称呼

156
00:06:52,067 --> 00:06:52,807
Playhouse.
过家家

157
00:06:52,807 --> 00:06:54,389
And yet it's considered.
然而这却被认为……

158
00:06:54,389 --> 00:06:55,670
How is that casual?
怎么能算是随便玩玩？

159
00:06:55,670 --> 00:06:59,194
Situationships are a scam because that's what a situationship is,
模糊关系是个骗局 本质上它就是：

160
00:06:59,194 --> 00:07:00,857
is one person is benefiting from the fact
一个人在利用另一个人不敢发声的现状

161
00:07:00,857 --> 00:07:02,317
that the other person is not speaking up.
来获利

162
00:07:02,317 --> 00:07:04,841
And then the other that's not speaking out is probably terrified
而另一个不开口的人 吓得不敢说

163
00:07:04,841 --> 00:07:07,225
of saying anything because they know what the answer will be.
因为他们知道答案是什么

164
